{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Shopping Spree"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Shopaholic"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about fashion."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Superlatives and Comparatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "  You use <span class=\"strong\">comparative adjectives</span> to make a comparison between two things or two people. When you make a comparison, you should use the word <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">than</span></span> after the <span class=\"strong\">comparative adjective</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br> <span class=\"italic\">She is tall<span class=\"strong\">er than</span> me. <br> The library is old<span class=\"strong\">er than</span> the museum.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With one syllable words, you add <span class=\"strong\">-er</span> to the adjective to make the <span class=\"strong\">comparative form</span>. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The best places are on Rose or Trinity. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They have the coolest little shops!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They're the priciest too!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You want to be the smartest looking writer, right!"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cheap\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cheap<span class=\\\"strong\\\">er</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new<span class=\\\"strong\\\">er</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tall<span class=\\\"strong\\\">er</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With  <span class=\"strong\">adjectives</span> of two or more syllables, you add the word <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">more</span></span> before the adjective."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective                    \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"expensive                   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> more</span>  expensive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"interesting                   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">more</span> interesting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" difficult   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> more </span> difficult\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can compare things using the words more (than) or less (than). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">superlative adjectives</span> to compare one thing or person among two or more things or people. When you make a comparison using the <span class=\"strong\">superlative form</span>, you should use the word <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">the </span></span>before the <span class=\"strong\">superlative adjective</span> . "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">She is <span class=\"strong\">the tallest</span>  in her class. <br> The library is<span class=\"strong\"> the oldest</span> building at the school.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With one syllable <span class=\"strong\">adjective</span> , you add <span class=\"strong\">-est</span>  to the <span class=\"strong\">adjective</span>  to make the <span class=\"strong\">superlative form</span> . "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective                    \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"cheap                           \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the cheap<span class=\\\"strong\\\">est</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"new                              \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the new<span class=\\\"strong\\\">est</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tall                                \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the tall<span class=\\\"strong\\\">est</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With <span class=\"strong\">adjectives</span> of two or more syllables, you add the words <span class=\"strong\">the most</span> before the <span class=\"strong\">adjective</span> ."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective                    \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"expensive                    \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">the most</span>  expensive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"interesting  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">the most</span>  interesting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"difficult                        \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">the most</span>  difficult\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Language for Comparing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When shopping, it is common to describe products or items by talking about particular qualities or features that they have.<br/><br/>It is also common to compare ourselves and the way we look in a garment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A comparative adjective is used to compare two people, places, ideas or things."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When comparing two items that are equal, we use the form <span class=\"italic\">as + adjective + as.</span><br/>Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\">This shop isn't <span class=\"strong\">as trendy as</span> the other one we went into.<br/>This sweater doesn't look <span class=\"strong\">as good</span> on me <span class=\"strong\">as</span> the other one.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "My clothes don't fit as well as they used to! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We haven't gone shopping as often as we did in college."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't want to look as old and stuffy as the other women. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I guess I can't afford to dress as cheaply as I used to. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wardrobe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the clothing a person wears"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I need to add some new clothing to my wardrobe. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overhaul"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change and improve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  My wardrobe needs an overhaul."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "purchase"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something you have bought "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My most recent purchases are months old. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to step up your game"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to compete at a higher level"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have to step up my game at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "uniform"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "clothing worn for certain jobs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm always in my work uniform."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stuffy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "formal; old-fashioned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't want to look as old and stuffy as the other women.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "two piece suit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pants and a jacket or pants and a skirt made of the same fabric"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The men all wear two piece suits to work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reinvent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do something new based on what already exists "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I feel like I have to reinvent my look. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "look"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way you present yourself fashion-wise"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Stars have to reinvent their look every year to stay current."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le07ob01aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le07ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find two pictures of two differently dressed people from a fashion magazine or online."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the differences between the clothes the people are wearing  (use as much clothing vocabulary as you can). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph of 100 words describing and comparing the clothes in the pictures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use comparative adjectives and <span class=\"italic\">(not) as ... as</span>."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I describe differences between the clothes people are wearing in two pictures."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use clothing vocabulary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write using comparisons."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about clothing."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can compare two things or people and describe the quality of an object or a person.  "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can make comparisons using <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span> and <span class=\"italic\">not as</span>."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you always shop in the same place or do you try different places? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What attracts you to a store? The styles ?The price? The quality? "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content"